{%- comment -%}
  GN RATING - ibBan
  {% render 'gn-rating' %}

  Rating pill rendered directly under the price by the custom_liquid_gnrating
  block. Redesigned 25 Sep 2026 from the "2a Rating pill" design: grey pill,
  black score badge with a gold star, a five-star row, the count, a chevron.

  IMPORTANT - BLOCK ORDER LIVES IN MORE THAN ONE FILE.
  Markets with their own theme customization keep their own block_order,
  which overrides the parent template:
      templates/product.json                        (Store default)
      templates/product.context.rest-of-world.json  (Rest of World, and the
                                                     markets nested under it)
  Any market customized later - United Kingdom, for one - will generate its
  own context file and will need "custom_liquid_gnrating" added after
  "price" in its block_order too.

  GN_RT_MODE decides what the pill shows:
    store  (current)  Always the shop-wide Judge.me aggregate, labelled
                      "store reviews" so it is never mistaken for this
                      product's own score. Roughly 40% of active products
                      have no reviews at all.
    auto              This product's own rating when it has reviews,
                      falling back to the store aggregate when it has none.

  Sources:
    shop.metafields.judgeme.all_reviews_rating / all_reviews_count
    product.metafields.reviews.rating / rating_count
  Judge.me refreshes the shop metafields periodically, not in real time.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  WHY THERE IS NO "VERIFIED BUYERS" IN THE PILL  (25 Sep 2026)

  The desktop design put "Verified buyers" next to the count. It was left
  out on purpose. Judge.me's own medals metafield
  (shop.metafields.judgeme.medals / verified_badge) certified 70 reviews as
  verified purchases, at 4.49 - against roughly 1,083 in the count. Printing
  "verified buyers" beside 1,083 claims something Judge.me itself does not.
  The mobile design had already dropped it. Per-review "Verified" ticks in
  the reviews section are fine - those read each review's own flag.
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  WHERE THE PILL GOES

  The design links the pill to the reviews section further down the same
  page, so that is what it does: if sections/gn-product-reviews.liquid is on
  the page (selector section.gnpr), a click scrolls there, clearing the
  sticky header. If it is not on the page - another template, or the section
  rendered nothing - the click follows the href to GN_RT_LINK, the reviews
  page. With JavaScript off, the href still works.

  URL BUILDING - DO NOT "SIMPLIFY" THIS  (fixed 20 Sep 2026)
  GN_RT_LINK is a path only. The market prefix comes from routes.root_url,
  which is "/" on the primary market and "/es-es", "/en-es" and so on inside
  the Spain market's subfolders. The first version used
      routes.root_url | remove_last: '/' | append: GN_RT_LINK
  remove_last strips the last '/' ANYWHERE in the string. On "/es-es" the
  only slash is the leading one, so it produced "es-es/pages/reviews" - a
  relative URL that resolved against the product path and 404'd. Append then
  collapse '//' is correct for "/", "/es-es" and "/es-es/" alike.
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  WIDTH ON PHONES
  The Spanish label ("reseñas de la tienda") makes the pill about 360px wide,
  which overflows a 375px phone. So under 430px the Spanish pill drops the
  five-star row - the badge still carries the score and a star - and every
  language drops it under 340px.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  LEGACY BLOCK OVERRIDES  (added 31 Aug 2026)

  Two older blocks in sections/main-product.liquid duplicate what the buy box
  now shows. Both are hidden by the two CSS rules at the top of the style tag
  below. That is a patch - the markup is still generated on every product
  page - so both should be deleted at source and these rules removed with
  them. Each is wrapped in its own START/END comment, so they are easy to
  find in Online Store > Themes > Edit code > sections/main-product.liquid:

    .recommended-size-range
        "START RECOMMENDED SIZE RANGE METAFIELD" ... "END"
        Sits just after {% render 'variant-picker' %} inside the
        {%- when 'variant-picker' -%} case, which is why the theme editor
        highlights it as part of the Variant picker block. It reads the same
        custom.best_suited_for metafield as the delivery widget's fit row.
        It was dormant until the metafield was filled in.

    .klarna-badge
        Inside the {%- when 'buy-buttons' -%} case, in the
        {%- unless bb_is_b2b -%} branch. This is the old pink "Pay in 3
        interest-free installments" banner, replaced by the Klarna row in
        the delivery widget. Once it is deleted, the JS sweep named
        killOldKlarna in gn-shipping-bar can go too.
        Note: a second .klarna-badge exists in the variant-picker case for
        B2B customers with a "row" tagged product. That one is intentionally
        left visible - this snippet does not render for B2B customers, so
        these rules never load for them.
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- capture jm_rating -%}{{ shop.metafields.judgeme.all_reviews_rating }}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- capture jm_count -%}{{ shop.metafields.judgeme.all_reviews_count }}{%- endcapture -%}

{%- liquid
  assign GN_RT_MODE = 'store'
  assign GN_RT_LINK = '/pages/reviews'

  assign rt_href = routes.root_url | append: GN_RT_LINK | replace: '//', '/'

  assign jm_rating = jm_rating | strip
  assign jm_count = jm_count | strip
  assign jm_ok = false
  if jm_rating != blank and jm_count != blank and jm_count != '0'
    assign jm_ok = true
  endif

  assign p_count = product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value | default: 0
  assign p_rating = product.metafields.reviews.rating.value.rating | default: 0
  assign p_ok = false
  if p_count > 0 and p_rating > 0
    assign p_ok = true
  endif

  assign rt_mode = ''
  if GN_RT_MODE == 'store' and jm_ok
    assign rt_mode = 'store'
  elsif p_ok
    assign rt_mode = 'product'
  elsif jm_ok
    assign rt_mode = 'store'
  endif

  if rt_mode == 'store'
    assign rt_val = jm_rating | plus: 0.0
    assign rt_count = jm_count | plus: 0
  elsif rt_mode == 'product'
    assign rt_val = p_rating
    assign rt_count = p_count
  endif

  assign rt_pct = rt_val | times: 20.0

  assign rt_lang = request.locale.iso_code | default: 'en'
  if localization.country.iso_code == 'ES'
    assign rt_lang = 'es'
  endif

  if rt_lang == 'es'
    assign t_store_reviews = ' reseñas de la tienda'
    assign t_reviews = ' reseñas'
    assign t_aria_a = 'Valoración '
    assign t_aria_b = ' de 5 sobre '
    assign t_aria_c = ' reseñas. Ver las reseñas'
  else
    assign t_store_reviews = ' store reviews'
    assign t_reviews = ' reviews'
    assign t_aria_a = 'Rated '
    assign t_aria_b = ' out of 5 from '
    assign t_aria_c = ' reviews. Read the reviews'
  endif

  if rt_mode == 'product'
    assign t_label = t_reviews
  else
    assign t_label = t_store_reviews
  endif
-%}

{%- if rt_mode != blank -%}
  <a
    href="{{ rt_href }}"
    class="gn-rt{% if rt_lang == 'es' %} gn-rt--long{% endif %}"
    data-gn-rt
    data-mode="{{ rt_mode }}"
    data-raw="{{ rt_count }}"
    data-rating="{{ rt_val }}"
    data-locale="{{ rt_lang }}"
    aria-label="{{ t_aria_a }}{{ rt_val }}{{ t_aria_b }}{{ rt_count }}{{ t_aria_c }}"
  >
    <span class="gn-rt__badge"><span data-gn-rt-num>{{ rt_val }}</span><span class="gn-rt__bstar" aria-hidden="true">★</span></span>
    <span class="gn-rt__stars" style="--gn-rt-pct:{{ rt_pct }}%" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="gn-rt__bg">★★★★★</span><span class="gn-rt__fg">★★★★★</span>
    </span>
    <span class="gn-rt__count"><span data-gn-rt-count>{{ rt_count }}</span>{{ t_label }}</span>
    <span class="gn-rt__chev" aria-hidden="true">›</span>
  </a>

  <style>
    /* Legacy blocks in sections/main-product.liquid - see comment at top.
       Delete these two rules once the source blocks are removed. */
    .recommended-size-range{ display:none !important; }
    .klarna-badge{ display:none !important; }

    .gn-rt{
      --gn-rt-star:#F2A93B; --gn-rt-empty:#D4D4D4;
      display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:12px;
      width:fit-content; max-width:100%; box-sizing:border-box;
      margin:12px 0 0; padding:6px 16px 6px 6px;
      background:#F6F6F6; border:1px solid #E5E5E5; border-radius:999px;
      color:#111111; text-decoration:none; white-space:nowrap;
      font:inherit; font-size:14px; line-height:1; cursor:pointer;
      font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums lining-nums;
      transition:border-color .15s ease;
    }
    .gn-rt:hover{ border-color:#111111; color:#111111; }
    .gn-rt:visited, .gn-rt:focus{ color:#111111; }
    .gn-rt:focus-visible{ outline:2px solid #111111; outline-offset:3px; }

    .gn-rt__badge{
      display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:4px;
      background:#111111; color:#FFFFFF;
      font-size:14px; font-weight:600; line-height:1;
      padding:6px 10px; border-radius:999px;
    }
    .gn-rt__bstar{ color:var(--gn-rt-star); }

    .gn-rt__stars{ position:relative; display:inline-block; white-space:nowrap; font-size:15px; letter-spacing:1.5px; line-height:1; }
    .gn-rt__bg{ color:var(--gn-rt-empty); }
    .gn-rt__fg{
      position:absolute; left:0; top:0; overflow:hidden; white-space:nowrap;
      letter-spacing:inherit; width:var(--gn-rt-pct, 0%); color:var(--gn-rt-star);
    }

    .gn-rt__count{ font-size:14px; font-weight:500; }
    .gn-rt__chev{ font-size:16px; color:#757575; line-height:1; }

    @media (max-width:749px){
      .gn-rt{ gap:10px; padding:5px 14px 5px 5px; min-height:44px; }
      .gn-rt__stars{ font-size:14px; letter-spacing:1px; }
    }
    @media (max-width:430px){ .gn-rt--long .gn-rt__stars{ display:none; } }
    @media (max-width:340px){ .gn-rt__stars{ display:none; } }
  </style>

  <script>
  (function(){
    if (window.__gnRt) return; window.__gnRt = true;

    function fmt(n, loc, dec){
      try {
        return dec
          ? n.toLocaleString(loc, { minimumFractionDigits: 1, maximumFractionDigits: 2 })
          : n.toLocaleString(loc);
      } catch (e) { return String(n); }
    }

    function headerOffset(){
      var max = 0;
      var els = document.querySelectorAll('sticky-header, header, [class*="header"]');
      for (var i = 0; i < els.length && i < 40; i++){
        var cs = window.getComputedStyle(els[i]);
        if ((cs.position === 'sticky' || cs.position === 'fixed') && (parseFloat(cs.top) || 0) <= 1){
          var h = els[i].getBoundingClientRect().height;
          if (h > max && h < 260) max = h;
        }
      }
      return max;
    }

    function onClick(e){
      var target = document.querySelector('section.gnpr');
      if (!target) return;
      e.preventDefault();
      var y = target.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.pageYOffset - headerOffset() - 8;
      try { window.scrollTo({ top: Math.max(0, y), behavior: 'smooth' }); }
      catch (err) { window.scrollTo(0, Math.max(0, y)); }
    }

    function wire(){
      var els = document.querySelectorAll('[data-gn-rt]');
      for (var i = 0; i < els.length; i++){
        var el = els[i];
        if (el.dataset.gnWired) continue;
        el.dataset.gnWired = '1';

        var loc = el.dataset.locale || 'en';
        var out = el.querySelector('[data-gn-rt-count]');
        var raw = parseInt(el.dataset.raw, 10);
        if (out && !isNaN(raw)) out.textContent = fmt(raw, loc, false);

        var num = el.querySelector('[data-gn-rt-num]');
        var rv = parseFloat(el.dataset.rating);
        if (num && !isNaN(rv)) num.textContent = fmt(rv, loc, true);

        el.addEventListener('click', onClick);
      }
    }

    if (document.readyState === 'loading') document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', wire);
    else wire();
    document.addEventListener('shopify:section:load', wire);
    var n = 0;
    var t = setInterval(function(){ wire(); if (++n >= 8) clearInterval(t); }, 1200);
  })();
  </script>
{%- endif -%}
